#! program build/docs-examples/bin/cb_markdown
#! args    ../../../docs/examples/data/cb_markdown.md
#! frames  370
#! poster  369
#! crop    0 0 1000 600
#! keys
# a link of a few lines of Markdown in the solver's window opens the help, a page from a Markdown file; a click in its
# table of contents scrolls to "Boundary conditions"; ctrl+f finds "pressure" (enter: the next match); escape closes
# the bar; back at the top, a click on the link to the project's site is reported to the program, which shows it on
# the last line: nothing is opened
0   move 200 300
10  move 111 74 15
30  down
32  up
50  move 404 135 20
80  down
82  up
130 move 760 300 15
150 key ctrl down
151 key f
152 key ctrl up
160 text pressure
200 key enter
240 key escape
260 move 380 78 15
280 down
282 up
310 move 770 123 15
330 down
332 up
